<title>NORWAY: CBK Q1 profits rise.</title>
<headline>CBK Q1 profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31</p>
<p>				(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Net interest income			884	vs	858</p>
<p> Non-interest income			511	vs	377</p>
<p> Non-interest expenses		    803	vs	737</p>
<p>Operating profit before</p>
<p> loan losses				  592	vs	498</p>
<p> Operating profit after losses	  692	vs	562</p>
<p> After-tax result			   685	vs	555</p>
<p> EPS Q1  (crowns)			  1,24	vs     1,01</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name is Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse, Norway's second biggest bank. It was expected to register first-quarter operating profits after losses of 494 million crowns, according to a forecast consensus by seven analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>Christiania plans to merge with Storebrand, Norway's biggest insurance company, this year to form the biggest financial institution in the country.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
